The Service Desk Manager oversees a number of key functions within the Operations Team that enables the delivery of a high-quality service to end users. The role requires ability to multi-task with many activities occurring simultaneously, which requires excellent leadership, time management and prioritization skills.
A typical day for a Service Desk Manager will be a combination of planned activities, operational monitoring, and involvement in escalations and process exceptions.
This position is a stakeholder facing role and requires that you establish and manage expectations within the business and drive the Service Desk Team to achieve those expectations to a high standard.
Responsibilities:
Oversee the day-to-day operations of the IT Service Desk team Review – including monitoring and evaluating operational metrics and note areas for attention. The manager will review metrics and reports throughout each day to adjust staffing and workflows as needed to optimize the Service Desk performance.
Address SLA areas of concern. Evaluate/monitor closely on the Key SLAs to ensure fulfillment at the end of the month.
Monitor incoming tickets and calls to understand broad trends and identify dependencies that individual agents can’t see when working on an individual ticket.
Able to develop contingency plan if there are major incidents, manpower shortage, scheduled outages, and/or business events.
Follow up, review and attend to customer-satisfaction issues and user-feedback responses on a regular or timely basis.
Prepare reports. Able to analyze data to identify trends and areas for improvement and able to produce accurate management reporting on IT Service performance.
Drive internal and third-party service review meetings covering performance, service improvements, quality and processes.
Make recommendations for Service Improvement Plans and ensure actions are followed through to completion in a timely manner.
Staff Management including duty roaster, recruitment, mentoring, training, target setting and performance assessment.
Any other ad-hoc tasks when required by the Management.
Qualities and Skills required:
Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, including reporting and presentation skills;
A Service Management professional / Experiences in servicing / supporting Premium Retail customers;
Experiences in supporting regional customers is an advantage;
A passion for Service Improvement;
Proven track record in managerial grade, 2+ years of team management (managing a team with at least 20 staff);
Good knowledge of ITIL disciplines. PMP is preferred;
Willingness to support and mentor junior staff;
Able to work under pressure and meet deadlines;
Proactive, excellent leadership skills, self-motivated and able to take ownership.

