The position is responsible for assisting the Chief Risk Officer / SGM, GRCI in all aspects of the risk delivery. The person will work closely with CRO/SGM, GRCI, implementing Enterprise Risk Management Framework focusing on tier 1 & 2 risk reporting i.e. Strategic, Operational & Projects Risks, subsidiaries & HQ risks and Business Continuity Management. The person shall also assist the CRO / SGM, GRC in other strategic initiatives. The person shall coordinate with other functional areas in the Company particularly business units to ensure all risks in the Company are identified, measured, mitigated/ managed, and monitored/ reported.
Work closely with CRO/SGM, GRCI to ensure Group risk policies and operating models are appropriately localized and implemented;
Assist the CRO/SGM, GRCI in matters pertaining to Risk, Sustainability and Governance Committee (RSGC) reporting, e.g. Risk Management quarterly reporting, data pull, and trend;
Identify risks and their indicators in risk reporting and monitoring, addressing mitigation plans;
Facilitate an analysis of the financial and non-financial impact when risks occur;
To partner with the Head of Group Services and Head of Business Units to ensure that all Operational Risks (Tier 1 & 2) risks including investment & project risks, top risk and top emerging ESG & ABC risk identification and mitigation, implementation of appropriate risk management systems and loss event database are properly identified, quantified, managed and monitored;
To partner and collaborate with other Lines of Defence i.e. Internal Audit, Compliance, and Integrity Unit & Sustainability to implement an integrated operational risk management framework, including regular updates and tracking of the Risk and Compliance Assessment process, Internal Audit plan, and reports, Compliance / Integrity Unit’s top risk and top emerging ABC & ESG risk identification and mitigation, implementation of appropriate risk management systems and loss event database;
Be the subject matter expert and change agent on Risk Management;
To review and provide an independent assessment view on the key risks associated with projects undertaken
Environmental scanning to help identify emerging risks that may impact the organization arising from changes in the external environment;
Execute the implementation of Risk Management digitization, use of analytics, Machine learning, and Automation;
Assist in developing outreach and engagement activities in support of embedding and strengthening risk management culture and awareness;
Delivering impactful risk management training;
Deliver risk management training syllabus and propose recommended professional certification to be undertaken by all Teams;
Participate in outreach activities, including the Risk Forum and top management across the Group;
Other business units/functions – Execute and deliver initiatives on a regular basis to identify unique/emerging risks and design risk management strategies to address the risks identified;
Perform independent risk review and validation for any request on the Group’s undertakings;
Assist in developing Operational risk reporting/dashboard, timely communicate/escalate risk events, issues, and compliance with risk policies and limits to key stakeholders in the Company and in the region; manage the Company’s quarterly risk reporting;
Regularly review the Risk Management Framework, Business Continuity Management Framework, and operating structure for identifying, assessing, managing, and monitoring risks;
Execute the annual Risk Management processes with key business units, and stakeholders, update the risk assessment, and ensure adequate measures are in place to mitigate the identified risks;
Monitor the risk appetite, identifying key risk management strategies, assessing and profiling the key risks affecting the achievement of the business plans at group, business division, and at department levels;
Develop, refine, and review the Risk Register and evaluate the relevance of risks identified across business units in the Group;
Assist the Senior Management team in improving risk management / mitigating strategies and techniques, and carrying out follow-up action plans and their effectiveness in mitigating/controlling risks;
Review and evaluate the effectiveness of the implementation of action plans for risk management – provide assurance on whether the risk mitigation process is being driven effectively and efficiently, whilst also continuously monitoring whether the risk register is being updated appropriately;
Evaluate and draw attention to possible gaps in the risk register to the Senior Management and Head of Business Units - follow up on the development of control environment to overcome deficiencies in the risk management/mitigating process;
Collaborate working with relevant functions (e.g. Risk Management, Internal Audit, Finance, and Legal) to build up and/or implement a risk control framework (i.e. compliance self-assessment) and provide quality and solutions-focused advice on risk and control issues relevant to the business division for informed decision-making on compliance and ethics matters;
Provide oversight on Group Business Continuity Management program, initiatives and activities.
REQUIREMENTS:
Degree in Business, Law, Finance, Management or related fields
Strong technical risk management and proven ability to implement practical risk management processes and frameworks.
Knowledge of prevailing corporate governance requirements.
Solid financial and commercial acumen and understanding.
Excellent presentation skills and experience planning and facilitating workshops/risk exercises with senior level audiences.
Experience in ERM & knowledge of Risk Management Standards such as ISO 31000.
Robust diligence and ability to pay close attention to detail, including impeccable report-writing skills.
Must demonstrate the ability to handle multiple and conflicting priorities, and work under strict deadlines.
Should be an effective communicator with the ability to handle both internal and external communication.
Should demonstrate the ability to identify and respond to risk areas within the department.
Have experience in executing BCM deliverable

Review technical information;
Plan project schedule and assign resources according to scope of work;
Control and monitor UHP and ducting material, project cost, quality, and time;
Execute project according to plan and record changes to plan;
Prepare project deliverables and reports;
Perform inspection and testing for installation works;
To follow-up punch list closure to make sure testing can carry out without obstruction;
Liaise with clients, authorities, subcontractors, workers, and HQ office for project related tasks;
Maintain company’s management and EHS system at the project site.
