Job Description:
•    Managing the entire credit application process from application to providing recommendations to the approving committee;
•    Assessing credit worthiness of the credit applications, analysing current risks and identifying potential risks that could impact the company;
•    Communicate within the departments in assessing and establishing credit limits as well as determining its financial eligibility to the financing;
•    Implementing an overall risk management process for the organisation, which includes an analysis of the financial impact on the company when risks occur and provide on-the-ground solutions for it;
•    Leading a due diligence to the relevant parties involved i.e. Client, Contract Awarder, Supplier by meeting, calling and visiting;
•    Supervising the team members in handling the processing of the credit applications including legal documentation relevant to the financing;
•    Equal distribution of credit portfolios based on limit and nature of the contracts within the team whilst working with other department to achieve efficiency;
•    Overseeing the general health of the financing portfolio including periodic check on the repayment and the contract performance, which will include liaising with the Client, Contract awarder and Supplier;
•    Participate in enhancement of operational risk policies to minimise credit losses and preventing failed internal control processes;
•    Monitoring the performance of the team against the key performance indicators set; and
•    Develop and drive a sound, open and pro-active risk culture, working closely and collectively with functional units to support management in ensuring all key risks are reported and properly managed.
Job Requirements:
•    Minimum Bachelor's Degree holder in Accounting, Finance, Economics, Business, Law, Banking or equivalent qualification
•    Holder of professional qualification in Accounting, Finance, Banking, Credit and Investment Management field such as ACCA, CIMA or CFA is preferred
•    Strong analytical and problem solving skills in the field of accounting and finance
•    Knowledge in financial products offered by non-bank financial services such as Factoring, Insurance, Leasing, Trade Credit business or in other sub-sector of finance field such as investment or asset management will be an added advantage
•    Minimum 5 years work experience in the areas of credit management, risk management, risk control, business proposal and credit evaluation or similiar loan and transaction approving role
•    Strong leadership skills and able to motivate the team
•    Good report writing skills including preparing presentation on portfolio requirements to the management committee
•    Good command of spoken and written English and Bahasa Melayu
•    Ability to work independently and take initiative to communicate with other department colleagues including clients to troubleshoot matters.

