Company
INTCO is a global leading manufacturer and provider of total solutions for renewable polystyrene (PS) foam plastics. In the past 17 years, we are committed to the efficient collection, high-tech regeneration, and green application of renewable polystyrene to high-tech polystyrene pellets and eco-friendly polystyrene moulding for home decoration use.
With the world’s leading automatic equipment and high technologies, INTCO collects, regenerates and reuses over 50,000 tons of renewable polystyrene foams every year from worldwide saving 2 million trees and 150,000 tons of oil a year. This innovation and concept of transforming the “White Pollutions” into high-tech pellets and fine wall decor products have been awarded by many national governments and worldwide environmental associations.
In the early of June 2017, INTCO decided to invest and established a PS recycling plant in Malaysia. With just a few months the factory begin it’s operation during the end of March 2018 and currently having 8 production line with production capacity of 140 tons of plastic pellets a day. Besides continuous expansion of our polystyrene recycling business, we had also started the polyethylene terephthalate (PET) recycling project in Malaysia, setting up a new plant and diversifying our recycling capability.
