Job Description
UIG Architects Sdn Bhd is a fully registered architectural practice providing a wide range of architectural, design and project management consultancy services seek qualified individuals to join us as:-
Graduate Architect
Experienced Architect candidates are encouraged to visit our website for project information. Candidates who have independently delivered quality standard design drawings and project management are invited to submit their resume, portfolio and certificates.
Job Responsibilities:
Perform the role of an Architect in design and project management for residential, mixed development, commercial or master plan environment;
Conduct feasibility studies, prepare concept and schematic design drawings, design development, construction detailed drawings and building contract drawings;
Prepare tender documentation, schedules and material specifications;
Liaise with Client Representatives and Consultants at meetings to ensure project objectives are met;
Perform administrative and professional architectural works by managing projects from inception through implementation stage;
Lead and manage a team of architectural personnel consisting of Architects, Engineers, Designers and external Consultants to drive building excellence in architectural practices; and
Ensure design quality and works are carried out to the specific standards, building codes, guidelines and regulations.
Job Requirements and Conditions:
Candidate must possess, both degrees, Bachelor and Master Degrees in Architecture (total 5 years of studies separately or continuously) and has minimum 3 years working experience in similar position as in design and project architectural. Salary Offer depends on working experience;
Candidate registered with Board of Architects Malaysia/LAM is added value to candidate’s application;
Able to develop and maintain strong client relationship and has excellent time management skills to meet tight timelines;
A Good Team Player with a strong sense of responsibilities, highly energized, independent and pleasant personality;
Good in articulation and writing skills. Able to think strategically and lead a design/documentation team;
Conversant with local codes and Malaysian Authority approval processes;
Good knowledge of design development, tender detailing and construction practices in high-rise and commercial buildings or master planning projects;
Experience in project management processes, able to co-ordinate and direct other consultants in all phases of architectural services;
Required language (s): Ability to speak and write in English and Bahasa Malaysia proficiently;
Software skill(s) requirement: Sketchup 3D modelling, MS Office application, MS Project, Adobe PhotoShop, AutoCad, Revit, MS Power Point, Lumion or any Rendering Software; and
Possess own transport is an added advantage.
Benefits provided are:
Employees Engagement Programs;
Insurance coverage: Group Hospitalisation Insurance, Group Term Life Insurance;
Discretionary bonus based on Company's & employee's performances; and
LAM and PAM Membership Renewal for Graduate Architect.
Interested candidates are invited to email the following documents to the Human Resources Manager:
A comprehensive CV or resume demonstrating your skills, experience and LAM registration number;
Current and expected salary;
A concise portfolio of past works (MUST be in PDF file less than 8MB, A3 paper size, between 7 and 10 pages) that demonstrates your approach to design and commitment to quality;
Copies of ALL academic certificates ie. SPM/Form 5, Matrix / STPM, MUET, Bachelor and Master Degree or College Technical/Professional certificates;
Copies of Result Transcripts (Bachelor and Master); and
A PDF Copy of your MySejahtera Digital Certificate (Covid-19 Vaccinations Record).
Other positions such as Assistant Architect and Accounts Executive are available.

