DIGITAL ASIC DESIGNER
Microtest operates in the electronics field and is a provider of electronic device testing solutions. It was established in 1998 and over time has become a technology and innovation partner to some of the world's semiconductor leaders.
Microtest's Headquarter is in Altopascio (LU) . Microtest has subsidiary in Malaysia serving the Far East market.
Microtest employs more than 180 people.
Job Description:
The Digital ASIC Designer is a professional who collaborates on the development of application-specific integrated circuits (ASICs) by implementing the digital core. He/She optimizes the design according to customer’s specifications, generates the digital core of products and collaborates with the central ASIC design team in order to provide customized and competitive integrated solutions.
Duties & Responsibilities:
Hands on experience in all aspects of the chip development process with proficiency in front end tools and methodologies;
Development of front-end implementation tasks, such as VHDL/Verilog coding, synthesis, timing simulations and logic equivalence checks;
Management of Back-end phase (place & route phase and post layout simulation);
Responsible for validating and qualifying components through simulation, hardware emulation and laboratory equipment;
Pre-layout and post-layout functional and timing problem solver.
Technical Requirements:
Master Degree in Electronic Engineering,
working experience in ASIC area is preferred;
Expertise in HDL programming, logic synthesis, clock trees optimization, design for testability (DFT), digital synthesis, timing analysis, debug and validation;
Fluent spoken and written English.
Soft Skills:
Professional and pleasant personality with good written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills;
Able to work under tight deadlines in a fast paced environment.
Job Location:
Melaka, Malysia

GENERAL PURPOSE OF THE JOB
The role of this position includes providing financial, administrative and clerical support to the Company. You are required to process, verify and reconcile invoices. You are responsible to review all account payable transactions, liaising with vendors, ensure the accuracy of accounts payable reports and ensure all unpaid invoices are processed. This position also required to assist superior in accounting operations including designing, implementing and maintaining effective accounts payable, accounting policies and SOX Controls. You will report to Assistant Manager, Account Payable and work with teams of other departments such as Procurement and Operation.
SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES:
Yes
ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
The following duties and responsibilities generally reflect the expectations of this position but are not intended to be all-inclusive.
Prepare and ensure timely payment for suppliers/creditors for all DaVita Malaysia centers;
Supervise Account Payable team, review the transactions done by Executives and ensure all invoices are accurately coded for accounting purpose and adequately approved per the Approval Matrix
Assist in preparing, as and when required, the monthly closing report of Account Payable and ensure the accuracy of the reports;
Supporting knowledge transfer among team members and delivering trainings
Work closely with procurement, facility and operation team to ensure PO, DO & Invoices are received and endorsed;
Assist in daily full set accounting functions; including payment reconciliation follow-ups, attend AP-related inquiries from other departments or vendors
Assist in closing of monthly & yearly management accounts; working with internal and external auditors (respond to queries & provide documents)
Posting daily and month end transaction to ensure that transactions are captured in the accounting system in a timely manner;
Verify and ensure completeness of new vendor registration documents, set up and amend accounts payable vendors in Oracle system
Perform monthly supplier reconciliation;
Maintain and keep a proper filing of all documents;
To perform other ad hoc assignments as required.
MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS
Education, licenses, certifications, and experience required to fulfill the essential duties, including computer skills as required
Degree/Diploma in Accounting or equivalent;
Min 3 years relevant working experience, experience from a shared-service company will be advantageous;
Hardworking, meticulous, and detail oriented;
Multitasking, problem-solving skills, team player;
Good knowledge in Microsoft Office;
Self-starter, highly independently.

Main purpose
Responsible for leading the National School’s strategic direction, under the guidance of the Campus Principal. Maintaining high standards in teaching, learning, and overall school performance, ensuring adherence to educational policies and guidelines set by relevant authorities, and XCL Education. Emphasising academic excellence, while overseeing curriculum implementation, monitoring teaching quality, and fostering a conducive learning environment. Staff management and development, encompassing the professional duties of the teaching staff, performance evaluations, recruitment, and coordination of training needs. Active engagement with parents and pupils, promoting satisfaction and success.
Major Responsibilities
To provide and lead the strategic direction for the National School in line with the whole school vision and development plan and as directed by the Campus Principal;
To contribute to the school Strategic Plan.
To ensure that the standards of teaching, learning and attainment in all areas of school life within the National School reflect the school’s mission of providing the best of National education;
To ensure that the National School is operated in accordance with the policies, guidelines, procedures and approved recommendations of MOE, CAIE and XCL Education Group;
To ensure that appropriate priorities and targets for the improvement of pupils’ learning, are identified and the necessary resources are clearly allocated;
To ensure the management, organization and administration of the National School supports the improvement of standards in learning and teaching;
Manage change within the National School judiciously;
Inspire stakeholder confidence in the National School.
Academic and Curriculum
Promote and maintain an environment within the National School that secures high standards of planning, organisation, teaching, learning, behaviour and achievement;
Implement the CAIE and REAL curriculum in a way that is relevant to the needs of the pupils and enables all pupils to achieve;
Monitor and evaluate the quality of teaching and standards of learning and achievement of all pupils in National School;
Maintain and develop the National School’s extended curriculum and extra-curricular programme in collaboration with the Head of CCA and Sports;
Maintain and promote effective partnership with National pupils’ parents to support and improve pupils’ achievement and personal development;
Work closely with Examination Unit to ensure strict compliance to the examination standard as specified by CAIE/ School;
Plan for manpower allocation and prepare the school timetable before the new academic year starts;
Review an finalise the book list together with teachers before
Plan the school academic calendar with the Campus Principal before commencement of new academic year.
Staff Management
Ensure the professional duties of all teachers and teaching assistants within the National School, as defined in the terms and conditions of staff contracts, are fulfilled;
Plan, allocate, support and evaluate work (e.g. teachers’ observations at least twice a year and etc.) undertaken by groups, teams, individuals within the National School, ensuring clear delegation of tasks and devolution of responsibilities;
Ensure systems are in place for the performance management of National School staff and that their effectiveness is monitored;
Develop open and honest relationships with all staff providing information, support and objective advice as appropriate;
Work with the Principal to manage the recruitment of National School staff of the highest caliber;
Identify and propose training needs of National teachers and to take a lead role on the coordination of staff training.
Customer Service
Provide interface with parents and pupils to ensure satisfaction and success;
Ensure that parents and pupils are well informed about the curriculum, attainment and progress towards their targets;
Guide teachers to provide quality teaching service to parents and students;
Support Marketing Department in promoting National programmes to prospects and other National schools.
Other dimensions of Job
Monitor and review the use of resources in order to ensure the principles of best value are achieved within the National School;
Manage the school physical environment efficiently and effectively ensuring the school is a safe, healthy and attractive place for learning;
Set appropriate priorities for the expenditure of the National budget;
Support the school’s annual events eg. Open Day, Sports day, Parents’ Day, Teachers’ Day and etc., as and when required;
Represent the school on meeting up with relevant authorities and establish good rapport with them in the absence of the Principal;
Ensure the compliance of ISO requirements by the National School;
Attend to the needs of any other ad-hoc events that will involve the National School;
Work closely with the Head of international School to ensure that all expectations, standards, procedures and systems are built on throughout the school and ensure a smooth progression for pupils and staff between the two schools;
Work closely with the Campus Principal, Head of International and the Administration Staff on all operational matters related to the smooth running of the National facilities;
Provide information, objective advice and support to the Campus Principal to enable him/ her to meet his/ her responsibilities.
Take on teaching responsibilities of at least one National subject.
Deputise for the Campus Principal as necessary
Other duties as and when required by the school.
Requirements
At least a Degree in Education or equivalent.
5 years of work experience in similar capacity.
In-depth understanding on National/ national school capacity.
Possess communication, management and supervisory skills.
Proficient in English.
Strong ability to lead, supervise and motivate a group of teachers.
Passionate in driving the core values of the XCL Education Group to all levels and strong desire to ensure high standard of education.
Ability to implement strategic plans of the management to ensure success.
Ability to communicate effectively with all levels and disseminate instructions and information precisely yet clearly.
Pleasant and approachable with friendly disposition especially towards parents and students.

