JOB PURPOSE
This individual is to support the Manager in the smooth and efficient daily operation of the Student Finance and Timetabling Department, particularly in the Timetabling Unit with respect to all administrative functions related to annual university academic timetable and schedule of academic resources and facilities; academic services staff workload records; and provision of administration service to support core academic functions of the university. He/she is to support the Manager in the aspect of Exam Scheduling function as well.
KEY RESULT AREAS / RESPONSIBILITIES
1. To assist the Manager in handling of programme fee setup in CMS;
2. To assist the Manager on the allocation of the Faculty/School’s teaching space, timetabling and resource booking to match the requirements of the central timetable to the academic spaces and facilities available, in a timely manner;
3. To assist in meeting all service level commitments made to internal customers in Taylor’s as specified in a Service Level Agreement for the department;
4. Coordinate the process of preparing and producing the required timetable across the institution, working together with all the Faculty/School’s timetabling officers;
5. Assist in the resolution of cross Faculty/School’s scheduling issues;
6. In consultation with respective Faculty/School’s timetabling officers, to adjust the draft timetable to accommodate specific requirements and solve scheduling issues;
