The Malaysian Government’s call to public universities to operate more effectively and efficiently as corporate entities, saw the incorporation of the USAINS Holding Sdn Bhd (USAINS) in 1998 under the Companies Act 1965. As the corporate arm of Universiti Sains Malaysia (USM), it is tasked with developing income-generating businesses associated with the skills readily available within USM. USAINS Group of Companies is made up of USAINS Holding Sdn Bhd and three (3) active subsidiaries - USAINS Healthcare Sdn Bhd, USAINS Biomics Laboratory Testing Services Sdn Bhd and USAINS Infotech Sdn Bhd.
USAINS manages USM's extensive assets which include properties, projects, programs and enterprises either directly or indirectly through key subsidiaries, to make a positive contribution to USM and its wider community of USM. Each company in the group operate as a private company, limited by shares. The Holding Company is wholly-owned by USM, while the three (3) subsidiaries in turn are wholly-owned by the Holding Company.
It vision is to be recognized as the business of USM community that focuses on development of income generating activities either through our current core activities or new business ventures in areas consistent with the knowledge base and competencies of USM and USAINS.
USAINS Corporate Mission are :
1. For core businesses undertaken by USAINS, strengthen the business propositions for the services provided either to, or on behalf of the University and Industry.
2. Identify and develop new business propositions for consideration where USAINS and/or USM shall invest so as to generate new income streams and cash flow for sustenance for the University in the long term.
The USAINS' core strategy is engineered to meet its vision, mission and objectives. Each operating business unit of the USAINS Group of Companies is empowered to utilize the core competencies of the USM community and to market and engage with private industry and government agencies, always applying fair value propositions. The strategy is defined and driven through established the USAINS Business Plans.
It's Quality Policy is to only perform business activities within its defined core competencies. As a service based organization, we shall meet our quality obligations only when we have individually met each of our customer's requirement.
